From: NixOS maintainers <maintainers@nixos.org>
Subject: [PATCH] compiler_attributes: guard __attribute_const__ against glibc 2.42

glibc 2.42 defines __attribute_const__ in sys/cdefs.h. When kernel host
tools (resolve_btfids, etc.) include both the kernel header and a glibc
header, GCC 15 errors with "redefined [-Werror]". Add an #ifndef guard
so the kernel definition is skipped if already provided by the libc.

--- a/include/linux/compiler_attributes.h
+++ b/include/linux/compiler_attributes.h
@@ -80,7 +80,10 @@
  *
  *   gcc: https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Common-Function-Attributes.html#index-const-function-attribute
  */
-#define __attribute_const__             __attribute__((__const__))
+#ifndef __attribute_const__
+# define __attribute_const__            __attribute__((__const__))
+#endif

 /*
  * Optional: only supported since gcc >= 9
